## Workflow
- Implement this issue through verified completion without asking again for
  implementation approval. Preserve unrelated changes and technical prerequisites.
- Use the existing implementation; do not rebuild completed behavior.
- Verify the issue's acceptance criteria. Fixture checks do not prove live provider behavior.
- For recoverable failures, diagnose and fix the cause before ending the iteration.
- If more work remains, append exact progress and the next action to
  .ralph-tui/progress.md. Leave the issue unfinished; Ralph will retry it.
- Make routine implementation decisions autonomously and record them.
- If blocked by a material unresolved product decision or an external prerequisite,
  record the precise blocker with `bd update {{taskId}} --append-notes "..." --status blocked`.
  Do not signal completion or repeatedly retry an unavailable prerequisite.
- Use local Beads commands only. Do not push, pull, or run bd sync.
